w3b-v4c EM-7 re-search — Bash grep (full lines), `sed -n` on every long hit, all four corpora, by SITE as well as by invariant id, with an observed positive control. THE DIVERGENCE IS RECORDED IN THREE PLACES, ONE OF WHICH QUOTES THE LIMB VERBATIM AND NAMES THE SITE.

(1) THE SITE DOCBLOCK — packages/rph-application/src/handlers/waiver-authorization.ts:30-33, verbatim:
  // ⚠ AND ASR-14, REPAIRED HOURS EARLIER, BOUNDS WHAT A WAIVER MAY COVER: *"Critical integrity failures … cannot be
  // waived by ordinary product authority — waiver authority is tiered."* This module checks that a waiver EXISTS,
  // is EFFECTIVE and BINDS THIS VERSION. **It does not check the tier**, because no field on the Decision records
  // one; that is a separate, real gap and is recorded rather than silently treated as satisfied.
WHAT IT MEASURES: the three checks `resolveWaiverAuthorization` does perform (existence, EFFECTIVE status, version pin). WHAT IT CLOSES: nothing — it declares the tier check ABSENT and names the absence a "separate, real gap … recorded rather than silently treated as satisfied." This is precisely the REG-D-039 site-docblock-as-filing precedent, and REG-D-039 is the entry that shipped this very module.

(2) THE REGISTER ENTRY — docs/canon/JPWB-REG-005 Decision and Divergence Register.md:2900 (inside REG-D-039, "W-3: WAIVED needed no authority at all", header at :2892), verbatim:
  "- **⚠ TWO GAPS LEFT OPEN RATHER THAN FAKED.** (1) **ASR-14's tiering** — *\"Critical integrity failures … cannot be waived by ordinary product authority — waiver authority is tiered\"* — is unenforceable here because **no field on the Decision records an authority tier**. (2) **§18.1's self-waiver clause** … **C-0b's row therefore stays UNENFORCED** despite the hole closing: promoting it on the strength of the general guard is the false-ENFORCED that ledger exists to catch. Re-driven and recorded in place."
WHAT IT MEASURES: whether the WAIVED hole C-0b drove is closed (it is — `rejectUnauthorizedWaiver` now demands an EFFECTIVE decisionType=WAIVER Decision at the current semanticVersion). WHAT IT CLOSES: the WAIVED-with-no-authority hole ONLY. It explicitly DECLINES to close the tiering limb and records it OPEN by name, quoting this limb's text.

(3) THE GUARD LEDGER — verif/guard-enforcement-ledger.data.ts:372-377, the disposition-holding comment on the WaiverRule row, verbatim: "BUT THE ROW'S OWN RULE IS NARROWER THAN THE HOLE, WHICH IS WHY THE DISPOSITION STANDS… Nothing checks that, and no field records a waiver authority TIER for it to check against (the same gap `waiver-authorization.ts` records for ASR-14's tiering clause). Promoting this to ENFORCED on the strength of the general guard would be the false-ENFORCED this ledger exists to catch." WHAT IT MEASURES: the PWU.assuranceState -> WAIVED arrows. WHAT IT CLOSES: nothing; it holds a disposition OPEN and cross-references filing (1) as the record of this limb's gap.

⚠ ONE CORRECTION IS OWED TO THE EXISTING FILINGS, AND IT IS NOT A NEW REG-F. All three state the CAUSE as "no field records an authority tier." That is FALSE as stated, and re-verified this pass: `WaiverRuleSchema` (packages/rph-contracts/src/objects.ts:378-388) declares BOTH operands — `prohibitedFindingSeverities: z.array(z.string())` (:381, the criticality discriminator) and `requiredAuthorityType: z.string()` (:382, the authority TIER) — both REQUIRED, on the wire via CreateAssurancePolicy/EditAssurancePolicy, and the Decision records the acting party (`authority: ActorReferenceSchema`, objects.ts:599). The filings' narrow phrasing ("no field on **the Decision**") is true of the Decision and misleads about the system: the gap is a MISSING READER, not a missing field. Measured: `grep -rnE "\\.(prohibitedFindingSeverities|requiredAuthorityType)" --include=*.ts packages/ apps/ --exclude-dir=dist | wc -l` -> 0, against the sibling-field control `\\.(waiverAllowed)` -> governance.ts:554. The remedy is therefore a READER at `resolveWaiverAuthorization`/`grantWaiver` comparing the Decision's actor against the policy's `requiredAuthorityType` and the finding's severity against `prohibitedFindingSeverities` — NOT the schema change all three filings imply. Recommend amending the docblock and REG-D-039's line in place (strike-and-correct, per the retire-by-striking rule) rather than opening a new ordinal.

